{"name":"Fleur-De-Lis","hex":"#b090c7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fleur-de-lis","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A design representing a flower whose three petals are joined together at the bottom (⚜, ⚜️), often used in heraldry, where it is particularly associated with the French monarchy.","The main element in the logo of most Scouting organizations, representing a major theme in Scouting: the outdoors and wilderness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fleur-de-lis"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fleur-de-lis","blocks":[{"text":"The fleur-de-lis, also spelled fleur-de-lys, is a common heraldic charge in the (stylized) shape of a lily. Most notably, the fleur-de-lis is depicted on multiple flags of Quebec and on the traditional coat of arms of France that was used from the High Middle Ages until the French Revolution in 1789, and then again in brief periods in the 19th century. This design still represents France and its royal dynasty in the form of marshalling on the arms of other countries and jurisdictions, including Spain, Quebec and Canada."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Fleur-de-lis.svg/330px-Fleur-de-lis.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fleur-de-lis"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Clovis_recevant_la_fleur_de_lys_-_XVe_si%C3%A8cle.jpg/500px-Clovis_recevant_la_fleur_de_lys_-_XVe_si%C3%A8cle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Clovis_recevant_la_fleur_de_lys_-_XVe_si%C3%A8cle.jpg/500px-Clovis_recevant_la_fleur_de_lys_-_XVe_si%C3%A8cle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"15th-century manuscript depicting an angel sending the fleurs-de-lis to Clovis. From the Bedford Hours in the British Library, London.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClovis_recevant_la_fleur_de_lys_-_XVe_si%C3%A8cle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Fleur.iris.2.png/500px-Fleur.iris.2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Fleur.iris.2.png/500px-Fleur.iris.2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Iris compared with fleur-de-lis ornament[7]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFleur.iris.2.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Sumpf-Schwertlilie_an_der_Isar.jpg/500px-Sumpf-Schwertlilie_an_der_Isar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Sumpf-Schwertlilie_an_der_Isar.jpg/1280px-Sumpf-Schwertlilie_an_der_Isar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Sumpf-Schwertlilie_an_der_Isar.jpg/500px-Sumpf-Schwertlilie_an_der_Isar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Yellow Iris pseudacorus flowers on a blue field of water","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASumpf-Schwertlilie_an_der_Isar.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Stema_e_Karl_Topis%C3%AB.png/500px-Stema_e_Karl_Topis%C3%AB.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Stema_e_Karl_Topis%C3%AB.png/500px-Stema_e_Karl_Topis%C3%AB.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Albanian Prince Karl Thopia stone engraving of his coat of arms. (14th century)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStema_e_Karl_Topis%C3%AB.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Stema_e_Durazzove.png/500px-Stema_e_Durazzove.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Stema_e_Durazzove.png/1280px-Stema_e_Durazzove.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Stema_e_Durazzove.png/500px-Stema_e_Durazzove.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStema_e_Durazzove.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/TvrtkoIRevers.png/500px-TvrtkoIRevers.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/TvrtkoIRevers.png/500px-TvrtkoIRevers.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bosnian king Tvrtko I's gold coin (14th century) reverse – with the Bosnian state fleur-de-lis coat of arms. (GLORIA TIBI DEUS SPES NOSTRA)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATvrtkoIRevers.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Charlemagne-by-Durer.jpg/330px-Charlemagne-by-Durer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Charlemagne-by-Durer.jpg/330px-Charlemagne-by-Durer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Charlemagne, by Albrecht Dürer. The anachronistic coats-of-arms above him show the eagle and the French fleur-de-lis","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AImage-Charlemagne-by-Durer.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Coronation_of_Louis_VIII_and_Blanche_of_Castille_1223.jpg/500px-Coronation_of_Louis_VIII_and_Blanche_of_Castille_1223.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, 